Q('C2-L114','Integrated communication: Public discourse — the long speech',
 'eu consigo ler, ouvir, falar e escrever sobre o filibuster e a oratória maratona a partir da transcrição de um podcast, com ritmo e pausas bem marcados.',
 ('Reading · A podcast transcript',text('Podcast: “Words as Endurance”',['HOST: Today, the **filibuster**: the art of speaking **until the clock runs out**. In 1957, Senator Strom Thurmond **held the floor** for just over **twenty-four hours** against a civil-rights bill. **Reading** from, among other things, recipes and the Declaration of Independence, he **bought time** but **not the votes**; the bill **passed anyway**.','GUEST: What strikes me is that endurance **became the argument**. Nobody **quotes** what he said; they **remember** how long he said it. **That is the paradox**: a tactic **built on** words **empties** words of meaning.','HOST: So is it **rhetoric**, or **obstruction**?','GUEST: **Both**, and **that is why** it **divides** people. Supporters see **minority protection**; critics see **minority rule**.'],kicker='PODCAST',by='Transcript, edited',gloss=[('filibuster','obstrução parlamentar por discurso longo'),('hold the floor','manter a palavra'),('buy time','ganhar tempo'),('obstruction','obstrução')])),
 [('Thurmond’s speech stopped the bill from passing.','F','the bill passed anyway.'),('The guest says endurance became the argument.','T','endurance became the argument.'),('Everyone agrees the filibuster protects minorities.','F','critics see minority rule.')],
 [('“hold the floor” = ?',['manter a palavra','segurar o piso','varrer'],0,'held the floor.'),('“buy time” = ?',['ganhar tempo','comprar relógio','pagar a prazo'],0,'bought time.')],
 G('Argumentar em um debate oral',['Estrutura','Exemplo','Função'],[['**What strikes me is that…**','**What strikes me is that** endurance became the argument.','pseudo-cleft'],['**That is the paradox**','**That is the paradox**: words empty words.','destacar tensão'],['**both… that is why…**','**Both**, and **that is why** it divides people.','explicação'],['**whereas / while**','Supporters see X; **while** critics see Y.','contraste']],'No podcast, a fala usa **pseudo-cleft** (*What strikes me is…*) e **frases de ligação** para guiar o ouvinte. Faça pausa antes da ideia central.',warn='*Filibuster* é substantivo e verbo: *He filibustered the bill.*'),
 [('What ___ me is that endurance became the argument. (strike)','strikes','pseudo-cleft.',None),('He ___ the floor for twenty-four hours. (hold, passado)','held','verbo.',None),('That is the ___: words empty words. (paradox)','paradox','destaque.',None),('Supporters see protection, ___ critics see rule by a minority. (while)','while','contraste.',None)],
 V('legislative stalling=protelação legislativa|senate floor=plenário do Senado|talking filibuster=obstrução com fala contínua|marathon oration=oratória maratona|civil-rights bill=projeto de direitos civis|vote count=contagem de votos|cloture motion=moção de encerramento do debate|minority protection=proteção das minorias|majority will=vontade da maioria|obstructive tactic=tática obstrucionista|endurance feat=proeza de resistência|oral recital=recitação oral|recipe recital=recitação de receitas|record-length speech=discurso de duração recorde|parliamentary delay=atraso parlamentar|chamber rule=regra da câmara|debate clock=relógio do debate|bill passage=aprovação do projeto|passing vote=voto de aprovação|talk-out strategy=estratégia de esgotar o tempo|vote deadline=prazo de votação|time-buying move=manobra para ganhar tempo|empty rhetoric=retórica vazia|spoken marathon=maratona de fala|procedural weapon=arma procedimental|floor privilege=privilégio de fala|dissenting senator=senador dissidente|historical footnote=nota histórica|procedure amendment=emenda ao regimento|supermajority threshold=limiar de supermaioria'),
 ('Podcast studio',[('Host','Was the filibuster rhetoric or obstruction?','O filibuster era retórica ou obstrução?'),('Guest','Both. That is why it divides people.','Ambos. É por isso que divide as pessoas.'),('Host','What strikes you most about it?','O que mais lhe chama a atenção?'),('Guest','That endurance became the argument.','Que a resistência virou o argumento.')]),
 [('Use a pseudo-cleft.','Use.','What strikes me is the length of the speech.'),('Highlight a paradox.','Destaque.','That is the paradox of the filibuster.'),('Contrast two views with while.','Contraste.','Supporters see protection, while critics see obstruction.')],
 ('Write a 5-sentence podcast intro about a famous long speech, using What strikes me is…, That is the paradox and while.','Today we look at a speech that lasted over twenty-four hours. What strikes me is that nobody remembers a single line. That is the paradox of endurance as rhetoric. Supporters call it protection, while critics call it obstruction. Which is it? Let us find out.',['Usei **What strikes me is**','Usei **That is the paradox**','Usei **while**'],'5 frases'),
 verbs=[('filibuster','obstruir com discurso longo','The senator filibustered the bill.','O senador obstruiu o projeto com um discurso longo.')],
 expr=[('Hold the floor','manter a palavra'),('Buy time','ganhar tempo'),('Run out the clock','deixar o tempo se esgotar'),('Talk the talk','falar bonito'),('Walk the walk','cumprir o que diz'),('Beat around the bush','enrolar'),('Dig in one’s heels','empacar'),('Stonewall','obstruir'),('Go the distance','ir até o fim'),('Filibuster a bill','obstruir um projeto')],pron=RN)
Q('C2-L115','Integrated communication: Public discourse — a council hearing',
 'eu consigo ler, ouvir, falar e escrever sobre audiências públicas a partir de uma notícia curta, relatando posições e decisões com entonação adequada.',
 ('Reading · A short news report',news('Council Defers Vote on Waterfront Tower After Marathon Hearing',['The city council **deferred** its vote on the proposed Harbour Tower late on Tuesday, **after more than five hours** of public testimony. **Seventy-two residents** signed up to speak; **the last** took the microphone just before midnight.','Supporters argued the project would **create jobs**, while opponents **warned** it would **block** the view of the bay and **strain** local services. Council member Lia Moreno, **who chairs** the planning committee, said further **studies were needed**, adding that she **would not be rushed**.','The hearing will **resume** on 18 June. Meanwhile, the developer has **agreed to revise** the height of the building.'],kicker='LOCAL NEWS',by='City Desk',gloss=[('defer','adiar'),('testimony','depoimento'),('strain','sobrecarregar'),('resume','ser retomada')])),
 [('The council voted on the tower on Tuesday.','F','deferred its vote.'),('Seventy-two residents signed up to speak.','T','Seventy-two residents.'),('The developer refuses to change the design.','F','agreed to revise the height.')],
 [('“defer” = ?',['adiar','recusar','aprovar'],0,'deferred its vote.'),('“strain” = ?',['sobrecarregar','esticar corda','filtrar'],0,'strain local services.')],
 G('Relatar posições em notícia',['Verbo de relato','Exemplo','Matiz'],[['**argued**','Supporters **argued** the project would…','defesa de tese'],['**warned**','Opponents **warned** it would block…','alerta'],['**said / added**','She **said** studies were needed, **adding that**…','neutro'],['**agreed to**','The developer **agreed to** revise…','compromisso']],'Em notícias o verbo de relato tem **matiz**. Use **argued/warned/stressed** em vez de repetir *said*. Estrutura: *verbo + that + oração* ou *agreed to + infinitivo*.',warn='Concordância de tempos: *said she would not be rushed* (would, não will).'),
 [('The council ___ its vote until June. (defer, passado)','deferred','verbo.',None),('Opponents ___ that it would block the view. (warn, passado)','warned','relato.',None),('She said she ___ not be rushed. (would)','would','tempos.',None),('The hearing will ___ on 18 June. (resume)','resume','verbo.',None)],
 V('chamber ballot=voto em plenário|deferred vote=votação adiada|waterfront tower=torre à beira-mar|harbour tower=torre do porto|public testimony=depoimento público|speaker sign-up=inscrição para falar|midnight microphone=microfone da meia-noite|employment boost=impulso ao emprego|view corridor=corredor visual|bay view=vista da baía|local services=serviços locais|planning committee=comissão de planejamento|panel head=chefe da comissão|further studies=estudos adicionais|traffic study=estudo de tráfego|height limit=limite de altura|building height=altura do edifício|revised design=projeto revisado|developer’s offer=proposta do incorporador|resumed hearing=audiência retomada|marathon hearing=audiência maratona|five-hour session=sessão de cinco horas|council member=vereador|public comment period=período de comentários públicos|opposition group=grupo de oposição|neighbourhood league=liga de bairro|supportive letter=carta de apoio|zoning board=junta de zoneamento|permit application=pedido de licença|ballot measure=consulta por voto'),
 ('Newsroom',[('Editor','What did the council decide?','O que a câmara decidiu?'),('Reporter','It deferred the vote after five hours.','Adiou a votação após cinco horas.'),('Editor','Who spoke against the tower?','Quem falou contra a torre?'),('Reporter','Residents who warned about the view and services.','Moradores que alertaram sobre a vista e os serviços.')]),
 [('Report a decision.','Relate.','The council deferred its vote.'),('Report a warning.','Relate.','Opponents warned that traffic would worsen.'),('Report an agreement.','Relate.','The developer agreed to revise the height.')],
 ('Write a 5-sentence news report about a fictional public hearing, using argued, warned and agreed to.','The school board deferred its decision on Monday after a three-hour hearing. Parents argued that the change would help working families. Teachers warned that classes would be overcrowded. The superintendent agreed to publish a study before the next meeting. The hearing will resume on 3 September.',['Usei **argued**','Usei **warned**','Usei **agreed to**'],'5 frases'),
 verbs=[('adjourn','encerrar, suspender a sessão','The chair adjourned the meeting.','A presidente suspendeu a sessão.')],
 expr=[('Put to a vote','pôr em votação'),('Table a proposal','engavetar uma proposta'),('Carry the motion','aprovar a moção'),('Go on record','declarar publicamente'),('Raise concerns','levantar preocupações'),('Take a stand','posicionar-se'),('Sleep on it','refletir até amanhã'),('Kick the can down the road','adiar o problema'),('Lay out a case','expor um argumento'),('Hold a hearing','realizar uma audiência')],pron=AJ)
Q('C2-L116','Register: Professional — forms',
 'eu consigo reconhecer e produzir as formas do registro profissional (formal, preciso, sem coloquialismos) a partir de uma biografia profissional.',
 ('Reading · A short biography',bio('Camila Ferraz (fictional)',['Camila Ferraz is **Director of Communications** at a regional transport authority. **Prior to** joining the authority in 2016, she **served as** press officer for a university hospital, where she **led** the response to a major flooding incident.','She **is responsible for** public information, crisis protocols and relations with the media. Colleagues **describe her** as **measured, candid and exacting**. She **has authored** several guides on plain-language reporting and **regularly** addresses industry conferences.','Ms. Ferraz **holds** a master’s degree in public administration and **is fluent in** English, Spanish and Portuguese.'],years='born 1982',facts=[('Position','Director of Communications'),('Languages','English, Spanish, Portuguese'),('Specialty','Crisis communication, plain language')],gloss=[('prior to','antes de'),('exacting','exigente'),('authored','escreveu'),('fluent','fluente')])),
 [('Ferraz joined the authority before 2016.','F','joining the authority in 2016.'),('She is responsible for crisis protocols.','T','crisis protocols.'),('She speaks four languages.','F','English, Spanish and Portuguese.')],
 [('“prior to” = ?',['antes de','depois de','durante'],0,'Prior to joining.'),('“exacting” = ?',['exigente','exato só','cansativo'],0,'measured, candid and exacting.')],
 G('Formas do registro profissional',['Coloquial','Profissional','Nota'],[['get back to you','**revert** / **respond**','preciso'],['a lot of','**numerous / a considerable number of**','quantidade'],['before','**prior to**','preposição formal'],['look after','**be responsible for / oversee**','verbos de gestão'],['is good at','**is adept at / is skilled in**','competência']],'O registro profissional prefere **verbos precisos**, **voz ativa** com sujeito pessoal e **nominalização moderada**. Sem gírias, sem contrações em textos escritos formais.',warn='Formal não é obscuro: *utilise* e *use* têm o mesmo sentido; prefira o mais simples quando possível.'),
 [('___ to joining the authority, she served as press officer. (prior)','Prior','formal.',None),('She is ___ for public information. (responsible)','responsible','verbo de gestão.',None),('Colleagues ___ her as measured and candid. (describe)','describe','relato.',None),('She ___ a master’s degree in public administration. (hold)','holds','formal.',None)],
 V('director of communications=diretora de comunicação|transport authority=autoridade de transporte|press officer=assessora de imprensa|university hospital=hospital universitário|flooding incident=episódio de inundação|crisis protocol=protocolo de crise|media relations=relações com a mídia|public information=informação pública|plain-language guide=guia de linguagem simples|industry conference=congresso setorial|master’s degree=mestrado|public administration=administração pública|professional register=registro profissional|formal diction=dicção formal|measured demeanour=postura comedida|candid manner=jeito franco|exacting standard=padrão exigente|career summary=resumo de carreira|executive profile=perfil executivo|staff biography=biografia de equipe|line manager=gestor direto|chain of command=cadeia de comando|remit=atribuição|oversight role=função de supervisão|spokesperson duties=funções de porta-voz|briefing note=nota de orientação|stakeholder engagement=engajamento de partes interessadas|timetable outage=interrupção de horários|regional network=rede regional|appointment letter=carta de nomeação'),
 ('HR office',[('HR','Prior to 2016, where did Ms. Ferraz work?','Antes de 2016, onde a Sra. Ferraz trabalhava?'),('Manager','She served as press officer at a university hospital.','Foi assessora de imprensa em um hospital universitário.'),('HR','And her current responsibilities?','E suas atuais responsabilidades?'),('Manager','She oversees public information and crisis protocols.','Ela supervisiona a informação pública e os protocolos de crise.')]),
 [('Rephrase get back to you formally.','Reformule.','I shall respond by Friday.'),('Describe a role formally.','Descreva.','She is responsible for media relations.'),('Introduce a speaker.','Apresente.','Prior to joining us, she served as press officer.')],
 ('Write a 6-sentence professional biography of a fictional communications officer, in formal register.','Marcos Teles is Head of Media Relations at a regional health agency. Prior to joining the agency in 2019, he served as a reporter for a national daily. He is responsible for public information and press briefings. Colleagues describe him as precise and approachable. He holds a master’s degree in journalism. He is fluent in English and Portuguese.',['Registro profissional','Usei **Prior to**','Sem contrações'],'6 frases'),
 verbs=[('liaise','fazer a ligação, articular-se','She liaises with regional press.','Ela faz a ligação com a imprensa regional.')],
 expr=[('Prior to','antes de'),('Serve as','atuar como'),('Be responsible for','responder por'),('Take the lead on','liderar'),('Report to','subordinar-se a'),('Be fluent in','ter fluência em'),('Hold a position','ocupar um cargo'),('In an official capacity','em caráter oficial'),('Keep a low profile','manter discrição'),('Be well regarded','ser bem visto')],pron=RN)
Q('C2-L117','Integrated communication: Public discourse — a poem',
 'eu consigo ler, ouvir, falar e escrever sobre a força da voz pública a partir de um poema, atento à entonação e às imagens.',
 ('Reading · A poem',poem('Speech at Dusk',['The hall has emptied of its applause,','but one sentence lingers by the door,','like a coat that someone left behind.','','You said we would not turn away.','The windows took it, and the street,','and somewhere a child repeated it','to a dog that did not understand.','','Words are small, and yet they travel:','a seed of breath, a borrowed wing.','What we say once, in a hall of strangers,','we are asked to keep saying.'],by='Original poem',gloss=[('linger','demorar-se'),('seed','semente'),('borrowed','emprestada'),('wing','asa')])),
 [('The poem says the applause continues after the speech.','F','emptied of its applause.'),('A child repeats the sentence.','T','a child repeated it.'),('The poem ends by asking us to keep our words.','T','asked to keep saying.')],
 [('“linger” = ?',['demorar-se','sumir','gritar'],0,'lingers by the door.'),('“a borrowed wing” suggests…',['palavras ganham asas emprestadas','um pássaro roubado','um avião'],0,'metaphor.')],
 G('Imagem e ênfase no poema',['Recurso','Exemplo','Efeito'],[['símile','like a coat that someone left behind','compara'],['metáfora','a seed of breath, a borrowed wing','fusão de imagens'],['personificação','The windows **took** it','dá vida ao inanimado'],['enjambement','a child repeated it / to a dog…','fluxo entre versos']],'Em poesia, leia pelo **sentido**, não pela quebra de linha (*enjambement*): a voz **sobe** onde a ideia continua e **desce** onde termina.',warn='Não traduza palavra por palavra: **borrowed wing** é imagem, não literal.'),
 [('One sentence ___ by the door. (linger)','lingers','verbo.',None),('The windows ___ it. (take, passado)','took','personificação.',None),('A child ___ it to a dog. (repeat, passado)','repeated','verbo.',None),('Words are small, and ___ they travel. (yet)','yet','concessão.',None)],
 V('emptied hall=salão esvaziado|lingering sentence=frase que permanece|forgotten coat=casaco esquecido|dusk light=luz do crepúsculo|echoing corridor=corredor com eco|windowpane=vidraça|street echo=eco da rua|child’s voice=voz de criança|uncomprehending dog=cachorro sem entender|seed of breath=semente de sopro|borrowed wing=asa emprestada|spoken promise=promessa falada|strangers’ hall=salão de desconhecidos|repeated phrase=frase repetida|oral inheritance=herança oral|sound chamber=câmara sonora|whispered refrain=refrão sussurrado|poetic cadence=cadência poética|verse split=corte de verso|verse paragraph=parágrafo de versos|unrhymed lines=versos sem rima|final pair=par final|image cluster=conjunto de imagens|resonant ending=final ressonante|silent auditorium=auditório silencioso|quiet afterglow=brilho tranquilo depois|speech aftermath=rescaldo de um discurso|public memory=memória pública|promise kept=promessa cumprida|persistent echo=eco persistente'),
 ('Poetry circle',[('Teacher','What does the coat represent?','O que o casaco representa?'),('Student','The sentence that stays after everyone leaves.','A frase que fica depois que todos saem.'),('Teacher','And the child with the dog?','E a criança com o cachorro?'),('Student','Words travel even to listeners who cannot understand.','Palavras viajam mesmo para ouvintes que não entendem.')]),
 [('Read a line with rising then falling tone.','Leia.','Words are small, and yet they travel.'),('Explain a simile.','Explique.','The sentence is like a coat left behind.'),('Say what the poem asks of us.','Diga.','It asks us to keep saying what we promised.')],
 ('Write a short poem (8 lines) about a speech heard long ago, with one simile and one metaphor.','The hall is quiet now. One sentence stays, like a lamp left on. You said we must not wait. The promise is a bridge. We cross it every day. Some words are small. They grow when we repeat them. They grow into a road.',['Usei **símile**','Usei **metáfora**'],'8 linhas'),
 verbs=[('resonate','ressoar, ecoar','Her words still resonate.','As palavras dela ainda ecoam.')],
 expr=[('Echo through','ecoar por'),('Ring true','soar verdadeiro'),('Fall on deaf ears','cair em ouvidos surdos'),('Hang on every word','ficar preso a cada palavra'),('Words fail me','faltam-me palavras'),('A turn of phrase','um modo de dizer'),('Linger in the mind','permanecer na mente'),('Strike a nerve','tocar num ponto sensível'),('The ring of truth','o tom de verdade'),('Leave a mark','deixar marca')],pron=AJ)
Q('C2-L118','Integrated communication: Public discourse — the press conference',
 'eu consigo ler, ouvir, falar e escrever sobre coletivas de imprensa a partir de uma charge, identificando evasivas e respondendo com ênfase e ritmo adequados.',
 ('Reading · A comic strip',comic('The Non-Answer',[dict(scene='📸',bubbles=[('Reporter','Will taxes rise next year, yes or no?'),('Minister','What matters is that we are listening to families.')],cap='Panel 1'),dict(scene='🎙️',bubbles=[('Reporter','That was not a yes or a no.'),('Minister','I would rather not speculate; the figures are still under review.')],cap='Panel 2'),dict(scene='🙃',bubbles=[('Assistant','Sir, they have written “non-answer” on the board.'),('Minister','Excellent. Then they were listening.')],cap='Panel 3')],gloss=[('speculate','especular'),('under review','em análise'),('non-answer','resposta evasiva'),('board','quadro')])),
 [('The minister answers yes or no.','F','What matters is that we are listening.'),('The minister says the figures are under review.','T','figures are still under review.'),('The reporters think the answer was clear.','F','non-answer.')],
 [('“speculate” = ?',['especular','esperar','falar baixo'],0,'rather not speculate.'),('“non-answer” = ?',['resposta evasiva','resposta curta','sem resposta por falta de tempo'],0,'non-answer.')],
 G('Esquivar e responder',['Tática','Exemplo','Tom'],[['**redirecionar**','What matters is that…','evasivo'],['**adiar**','The figures are **still under review**.','neutro'],['**recusar especular**','I would rather **not speculate**.','educado'],['**responder direto**','**Yes, taxes will rise** by one point.','claro']],'Reconheça **evasivas** (*What matters is…, I would rather not…*) e saiba dar **respostas diretas**: sujeito, verbo, número.',warn='*Speculate* não é *especular* no sentido financeiro neste contexto; aqui é *conjecturar*.'),
 [('I would rather not ___. (speculate)','speculate','evasiva.',None),('The figures are still under ___. (review)','review','fórmula.',None),('What ___ is that we are listening. (matter)','matters','pseudo-cleft.',None),('Taxes ___ rise by one point. (will)','will','resposta direta.',None)],
 V('news conference=conferência de notícias|yes-or-no question=pergunta de sim ou não|evasive answer=resposta evasiva|scripted reply=resposta ensaiada|canned line=frase enlatada|media training=treinamento de mídia|bridging phrase=frase de transição|message discipline=disciplina de mensagem|hostile question=pergunta hostil|second-round query=pergunta de segunda rodada|pointed query=pergunta incisiva|tax rise=aumento de imposto|budget figures=números do orçamento|figures under review=números em revisão|ministerial briefing=entrevista ministerial|press pack=kit de imprensa|reporters’ pen=cercadinho dos repórteres|camera flash=flash de câmera|boom microphone=microfone de vara|live feed=transmissão ao vivo|image handler=assessor de imagem|damage control=controle de danos|non-committal reply=resposta sem compromisso|cagey response=resposta cautelosa|straight answer=resposta direta|candid admission=admissão franca|on-the-record remark=declaração oficial|background briefing=orientação em off|leaked figure=número vazado|headline quote=citação para manchete'),
 ('Press room',[('Reporter','Will taxes rise? Yes or no?','Os impostos vão subir? Sim ou não?'),('Minister','What matters is that we are listening.','O que importa é que estamos ouvindo.'),('Reporter','That’s not an answer.','Isso não é uma resposta.'),('Minister','Fair enough. The figures are under review.','Justo. Os números estão em revisão.')]),
 [('Deflect politely.','Esquive.','I would rather not speculate at this stage.'),('Give a straight answer.','Responda.','Yes, the rate will rise by one point.'),('Push for a direct reply.','Insista.','With respect, that was not an answer.')],
 ('Write a 5-sentence comic script in which a spokesperson avoids a question, then answers it directly.','Panel 1 — Reporter: Will the clinic close? Spokesperson: What matters is that we value patients. Panel 2 — Reporter: That is not an answer. Spokesperson: I would rather not speculate. Panel 3 — Reporter: Yes or no? Spokesperson: Fair enough. No, the clinic will stay open.',['Usei **evasiva**','Usei **resposta direta**'],'5 falas'),
 verbs=[('deflect','desviar, esquivar','Ministers deflect hard questions.','Ministros esquivam perguntas difíceis.')],
 expr=[('Dodge the question','esquivar-se da pergunta'),('Beat around the bush','enrolar'),('Pin down','fazer comprometer-se'),('Put on the spot','colocar contra a parede'),('Give a straight answer','dar resposta direta'),('Sidestep an issue','contornar um assunto'),('Toe the party line','seguir a linha do partido'),('Be economical with the truth','ser econômico com a verdade'),('Duck the issue','fugir do assunto'),('Press for details','insistir em detalhes')],pron=RN)
build_index();print('ok')
